          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ذعر — dhuʿr — \"panic, alarm\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "أصاب الناس ذعر بعد الزلزال. aṣāba an-nās dhuʿr baʿda az-zilzāl. Panic seized the people after the earthquake."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ذعر (dhuʿr) is built on the native Arabic root dh-ʿ-r, \"to frighten, to alarm\" (Lane). Dhuʿr is a sudden fright that runs through a crowd."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
