          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "أخاف — akhāfa — \"to frighten\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "أخافني صوت الرعد في الليل. akhāfanī ṣawt ar-raʿd fī al-layl. The sound of the thunder frightened me in the night."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Present: يخيف, yukhīf."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Do not confuse it with أخاف (akhāfa) read akhāfu, I am afraid, the present of خاف."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "أخاف (akhāfa) is built on the native Arabic root kh-w-f, \"fear\" (Lane). It is Form IV of khāfa, to be afraid: to make someone afraid. Mukhīf, frightening, is its participle."
            }
          ]
        },
